"""Deli Counter 0.266.0: an indoor litter bin stands against a wall -- the walker, walking cold run 9386: "garbage
cans are usually up against walls inside buildings" (the factory's `docs/findings/walk_2026-10-23_9386/`, finding 8).
`furnish` ends with `stand_bins_on_walls`, which moves each bin to the nearest clear spot flush against a wall of its
room and nothing else; the library's stored bins the same way (`migrations/migrate_bins_on_walls.py`).

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has been
worked out: `level_design.py` (anchored hunks); the new `tests/test_bins_on_walls.py` and
`migrations/migrate_bins_on_walls.py`; the 92 specs whose bins moved, each replaced whole; VERSION; the CHANGELOG
entry, prepended. Generated from a proven clone (`patches/dc_bins_on_walls/gen_dc_bins_on_walls.py`), dry-run on a
fresh clone to the clone's every byte, a second run refused (`patches/dc_bins_on_walls/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_dc_bins_on_walls.py
    cd deli_counter && python build.py --all && python nav_gate.py --all && python -m pytest -q && python check.py
"""
